  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e021a05c-0468-5ac3-9dda-9a76e8b60be2" activityNameId="5ef38dfa-a7a7-5307-b430-ff7b1b005782" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Facility of data center</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Facility of data center
The data center is constructed using typical materials found for the building of large IT facilities; UUID: c96074ca-7b22-31d1-9fa7-bc5f2cc902f7
The dataset is based on a description of a data center from a UK source from Whitehead et al 2015. Inputs are described with the unit kg/kW/year. To obtain the values in kg, the original input value needs to be multiplied with the IT power of the data centre, which is 12895 kW. Inputs described with Input-Output databases are not considered. The data center facility is based on a lifetime of 60 years. The amount of materials are based on the assumption that they should be replaced after 20 years.
Location: Global average data centers, though the source is based in the UK
Technology: Various construction materials are included in the inventory.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c96074ca-7b22-31d1-9fa7-bc5f2cc902f7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
